2. The definition of “work of engineering construction” in section 7(1) of the Factories Act includes the following works:
(a)the construction, laying, structural alteration, inspection, maintenance, repair, demolition or removal of —
(i)any pipe-line for the conveyance of water, gas or any other thing;
(ii)any drain, whether open or covered, except open drains situated in domestic premises; and
(iii)any underground electrical cable and communication cable;
(b)the inspection, repair or maintenance of any manhole, sump, inspection chamber, valve chamber, and any other similar confined structure providing access to pipe-lines or underground electrical cables and communication cables;
(c)the construction of any road or carpark; and
(d)the reclamation of any land.
